## §1 Observe

### Mechanics summary (census-priced, not digest-priced)
On black: the line "DESPITE THIS, CAPTIONS HAVE REMAINED UNCHANGED, SINCE 1971" stands crisp in small pixel type at the bottom (y≈0.875) while particles coalesce in four loose clusters at the numeral's top band → a formation front sweeps top→bottom: rows above the front are SOLID block-pixel glyph, rows below are falling particle rain → by ~24.0 s the numeral "1971" is fully solid (white block-pixel glyphs ≈70% frame width, ≈44% height, centre y≈0.47) with only residual specks at its bottom edges → clean static HOLD (no background particles visible) → exit somewhere inside 26.0–27.0 s (form unmeasured) into the next beat's particle band. One number carries the claim; nothing else moves during the hold. The digest's claim that the *line* "appears lettered in dissolving particles" is contradicted by the census (line crisp at the first black frame; the particles belong to the numeral) — census governs (departure D3 below). The register's "held ~3 s" is an estimate: measured legible span 24.0→26.0 = 2.0 s minimum (codex-observe finding 2).

