### Construction choice + rejected alternatives
**Chosen:** one self-contained HTML file, canvas 2D, ONE constant flow field (A5.4): every particle always carries the stream velocity along flow.directionDeg; FORM = borrowing onto runtime-sampled targets (A1.2: CONFIG.text.numeral rendered offscreen in a heavy monospace face, sampled on grid.sampleStepPx — the lawful letterform construction, T15 purity 100 precedent), borrow windows ordered by target row via time.frontSweepMs with per-particle seeded jitter so the front reads as coalescence, not a wipe; borrowed particles keep jitter (never zero velocity); reserve fraction never borrowed; unassigned surplus keeps streaming (never freezes — T15 convergent cure). LOCK: when a borrowed particle arrives, its cell takes over rendering as a solid filled rect at borrowOpacity and the particle returns to the stream (defines the census solid hold + the takeover the plan-review demanded); RELEASE starts from each cell's on-screen position with stream velocity continuity. Rendering states defined for every class: streaming-reserve (reserveOpacity), streaming-surplus (reserveOpacity), borrowing (borrowOpacity ramp), locked cell (borrowOpacity), released (borrowOpacity → reserveOpacity over exit). Phase machine PRE → FORM → HOLD → RELEASE → DONE is the single stage owner (A5 Cure 2 exclusivity survives reuse/restarts). Intensity separation (A5 Cure 1) rides the borrow flag and is asserted as an invariant (borrowOpacity > reserveOpacity; composited background dimmer than foreground) under palette swaps.
Rejected: CSS keyframes (no per-particle borrow/reserve state) · SVG draw-on (stroke register, not pixel cells) · DOM-per-particle (pool-scale perf, no canvas sampling) · traced bitmap / frame image (purity refusal class §6.1).

